                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_125\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes ArenaListener.onFoodLevelChange() so that, inside the\n`if (arena.isRunning())` branch, the event is only cancelled when\n`arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel`, instead of just `lockFoodLevel`. Without\nthe `inArena` check, the food-level lock applied to every player on the\nserver whenever any arena was running, not just players actually inside the\narena.\n\nTracing the history of this method:\n\n- In candidate_04/candidate_05 (initial ArenaListener implementation) and in\n  subsequent revisions up through candidate_97, onFoodLevelChange() used an\n  early-return guard:\n      if (!arena.isRunning()) return;\n      if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player) || !arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity()))\n          return;\n      if (lockFoodLevel) event.setCancelled(true);\n  This version correctly required the player to be `inArena` before cancelling.\n\n- candidate_125 refactors this method (to add \"food levels no longer deplete\n  for players in lobby/spectator area\", per its changelog entry) into:\n      if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player)) return;\n      Player p = (Player) event.getEntity();\n      if (arena.isRunning()) {\n          if (lockFoodLevel) {\n              event.setCancelled(true);\n          }\n      } else {\n          if (arena.inLobby(p) || arena.inSpec(p)) {\n              event.setCancelled(true);\n          }\n      }\n  In this rewrite, the `arena.inArena(p)` check that previously guarded the\n  `isRunning()` branch was dropped entirely \u2014 only `lockFoodLevel` is checked.\n  This is precisely the bug the fix commit addresses: the `isRunning()`\n  branch cancels food level changes for ALL players, not just those in the\n  arena, when lockFoodLevel is enabled.\n\n- candidate_128 is actually the fix commit itself (its diff hashes\n  9400d87..59c3b49 are identical to fix_commit_diff.txt), confirming that the\n  buggy code state (`if (arena.isRunning()) { if (lockFoodLevel) {...} }`\n  without the inArena check) persisted unchanged from candidate_125 all the\n  way to the fix, with no other candidate modifying onFoodLevelChange's logic\n  in between.\n\nTherefore candidate_125 is the commit that introduced the bug.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
